# Per-Dockerfile excludes for trail-admin. Combined with repo-root
# .dockerignore (BuildKit reads both — additive).
#
# admin-server only imports @trail/shared. It does NOT need engine
# source, drizzle migrations, pipelines, etc. Excluding aggressively
# trims context from 7 MB → ~1 MB.

# Engine source — admin proxies to engine via HTTP, doesn't compile its code
apps/server

# admin SPA: we only need dist/ (built by ship script). Skip everything else.
apps/admin/src
apps/admin/public
apps/admin/index.html
apps/admin/vite.config.ts
apps/admin/tsconfig.json
apps/admin/package.json

# Trail packages admin-server doesn't import
packages/db
packages/pipelines
packages/storage
packages/sdk
packages/core

# NOTE: apps/admin/dist/ambient (7.8 MB .opus sounds) + dist/thinking
# (460 KB) are now INCLUDED in the deploy context. Christian wants
# trail-sound feature on prod. F173 (Tigris) is the long-term answer
# for static media; until then we eat the 8 MB context cost per deploy.

# ─── Critical heavy excludes (F201.19) ────────────────────────────────
# BuildKit uses the per-Dockerfile ignore EXCLUSIVELY when present (it does
# NOT reliably merge the repo-root .dockerignore), so the big paths that
# root normally strips MUST be repeated here — otherwise /data (755 MB) and
# apps/ambient-capture/.build (1 GB Swift artefacts) land in the context and
# the transfer crawls past the builder deadline. None of these are COPYed by
# this Dockerfile (it needs only apps/admin-server, packages/shared,
# apps/admin/dist, and the lockfiles).
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.turbo
coverage
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
*.map
/data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
docs
apps/ambient-capture
apps/landing
apps/widget
apps/docs
apps/mcp
apps/model-lab
apps/onboarding
apps/web-clipper
apps/agent
apps/feedback-widget
adapters
